WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.069 --> 00:00:05.069
Fantastic Beasts And Where To Find Them has
more deleted scenes than any of the Harry

00:00:05.069 --> 00:00:07.430
Potter movies, according to producer David
Heyman.

00:00:07.430 --> 00:00:11.370
Yippee ki-yay movie lovers, it's Jan here,
and I'm going to talk about some of the deleted

00:00:11.370 --> 00:00:15.269
scenes that didn't make it into the first
Fantastic Beasts movie, as well as some of

00:00:15.269 --> 00:00:18.780
the things we can look forward to in the Fantastic
Beasts sequel.

00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:23.599
Of course, I'll be talking spoilers, so if
you're not ready for those, check out my spoiler-free

00:00:23.599 --> 00:00:25.689
Fantastic Beasts movie review here.

00:00:25.689 --> 00:00:30.849
Now, do you remember that little wisp of the
Obscurus that drifts up and out of the subway

00:00:30.849 --> 00:00:32.119
after the final battle?

00:00:32.119 --> 00:00:36.610
Well, although the Aurors thought they'd destroyed
the Obscurial, it was definitely a hint that

00:00:36.610 --> 00:00:39.480
we haven't seen the last of Credence Barebone.

00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:43.420
And there's actually a deleted scene that
would have made his setup for Fantastic Beasts

00:00:43.420 --> 00:00:44.980
2 a lot more obvious.

00:00:44.980 --> 00:00:49.170
In the scene Credence boards a boat, and it
seems like it might have been the one that

00:00:49.170 --> 00:00:51.780
Newt was getting on at the end of the movie.

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:55.201
Producer David Heyman has said they didn't
want to make the set-up of Credence for the

00:00:55.201 --> 00:00:59.980
next movie so obvious, but it feels like this
could have been a really good post-credits

00:00:59.980 --> 00:01:01.140
stinger.

00:01:01.140 --> 00:01:06.810
A scene cut early on in the movie featured
Jacob and his girlfriend, before he met Queenie.

00:01:06.810 --> 00:01:10.610
The scene had Jacob returning from the bank
to the street where he lives to find his girlfriend

00:01:10.610 --> 00:01:11.880
waiting for him.

00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:15.390
Director David Yates explained that in the
deleted scene "she runs down the street [and

00:01:15.390 --> 00:01:16.610
asks Jacob] 'How did it go?

00:01:16.610 --> 00:01:17.940
Did you get your loan?'"

00:01:17.940 --> 00:01:21.530
When Jacob replies that the bank didn't give
it to him, she takes off her engagement ring

00:01:21.530 --> 00:01:22.530
and leaves him.

00:01:22.530 --> 00:01:23.530
J.K.

00:01:23.530 --> 00:01:27.390
Rowling originally wanted the scene cut from
the final script, but Yates insisted on filming

00:01:27.390 --> 00:01:29.680
it as he thought it would be a touching moment.

00:01:29.680 --> 00:01:32.950
Yates said that it was cut in the end because
it was no longer needed to help the audience

00:01:32.950 --> 00:01:35.180
empathise with Jacob by that point.

00:01:35.180 --> 00:01:39.740
There's a really wonderful cut scene which
was teased in one of the trailers.

00:01:39.740 --> 00:01:45.020
The snippet we did see in the trailer is with
Jacob and Newt who are sat down in his menagerie,

00:01:45.020 --> 00:01:48.020
smiling and applauding with Jacob saying "I
wanna be a wizard."

00:01:48.020 --> 00:01:51.700
This was part of a much longer scene in which
Queenie and Tina sing the Ilvermorny school

00:01:51.700 --> 00:01:55.290
song as part of the discussion that Newt,
Tina and Queenie are having about whether

00:01:55.290 --> 00:01:58.380
Hogwarts or Ilvermony is the better wizarding
school.

00:01:58.380 --> 00:02:02.610
Alison Sudol who plays Queenie is a singer
as well as an actress and she wrote the song

00:02:02.610 --> 00:02:05.280
which both she and Katherine Waterston sang.

00:02:05.280 --> 00:02:08.970
Unfortunately, it slowed down the momentum
of the film and was cut, but David Yates has

00:02:08.970 --> 00:02:12.310
promised it will appear on the Blu-ray and
DVD extras.

00:02:12.310 --> 00:02:17.080
Originally, there was an extended version
of the scene at Macy's department store.

00:02:17.080 --> 00:02:20.720
While Jacob and Queenie were trying to catch
the Demiguise, which is charging around the

00:02:20.720 --> 00:02:23.830
store, it tramples over Jacob, who grabs on
to the creature.

00:02:23.830 --> 00:02:27.040
We then see Jacob getting dragged around by
something that's invisible.

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:31.170
Dan Fogler, who plays Jacob, has said the
moment is reminiscent of how Indiana Jones

00:02:31.170 --> 00:02:34.080
gets pulled around behind a truck in Raiders
Of The Lost Ark.

00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:38.300
The deleted scene finishes with a slapstick
moment as the Demiguise suddenly goes around

00:02:38.300 --> 00:02:42.770
a corner sending Jacob crashing into a clothing
display, and as Queenie runs over to check

00:02:42.770 --> 00:02:48.250
if he's OK, Jacob pulls on a hat and smiles
as if nothing had happened.

00:02:48.250 --> 00:02:52.210
Eddie Redmayne who plays Newt Scamander has
revealed that there was a shirtless scene

00:02:52.210 --> 00:02:56.500
that he had to spend seven months working
out for, but it ended up being deleted from

00:02:56.500 --> 00:02:57.670
the final film!

00:02:57.670 --> 00:02:58.670
J.K.

00:02:58.670 --> 00:03:01.620
Rowling had written in the script that Newt
needed to be buff in the scene which showed

00:03:01.620 --> 00:03:06.890
him into his briefcase and down into his menagerie
where he pulled off his shirt, revealing numerous

00:03:06.890 --> 00:03:08.500
war wounds and scars.

00:03:08.500 --> 00:03:13.810
So those were some of the scenes cut from
the theatrical release of Fantastic Beasts,

00:03:13.810 --> 00:03:18.040
but what do we know about what we can look
forward to in the Fantastic Beasts sequel!?

00:03:18.040 --> 00:03:22.450
Well, there are going to be four more movies
in the Fantastic Beasts franchise, each one

00:03:22.450 --> 00:03:23.840
set in a different city.

00:03:23.840 --> 00:03:28.950
The five movies take place over a period of
19 years, with the first film starting in

00:03:28.950 --> 00:03:31.990
1926 and the saga ending in 1945.

00:03:31.990 --> 00:03:37.450
Now, 1945 marks the year that Dumbledore and
Grindelwald had their epic battle that ends

00:03:37.450 --> 00:03:38.750
the Global Wizarding War.

00:03:38.750 --> 00:03:42.680
We already got the reveal of Grindelwald at
the end of this movie with a short cameo by

00:03:42.680 --> 00:03:46.940
Johnny Depp, and a young Dumbledore has been
confirmed to appear in the sequel, although

00:03:46.940 --> 00:03:49.550
at this point casting hasn't been confirmed.

00:03:49.550 --> 00:03:54.680
Dumbledore was born in 1881 so the actor playing
him could well be in his late 40s.

00:03:54.680 --> 00:03:58.200
Who would you like to see playing a young
Dumbledore in the sequels?

00:03:58.200 --> 00:04:02.690
Another storyline was teased for the sequel
thanks to the mention of Leta Lestrange mid-way

00:04:02.690 --> 00:04:07.200
through the film and again at the end when
Tina asked Newt more about Lestrange and he

00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:09.780
seemed to be evasive in his answers.

00:04:09.780 --> 00:04:14.820
Divergent series star Zoe Kravitz has already
been cast as Leta Lestrange and is confirmed

00:04:14.820 --> 00:04:16.750
to appear in Fantastic Beasts 2.

00:04:16.750 --> 00:04:20.880
It'll be interesting to see how her character
ties in with the Lestrange family from Harry

00:04:20.880 --> 00:04:25.530
Potter and also with the reveal in The Cursed
Child that Bellatrix Lestrange is the mother

00:04:25.530 --> 00:04:26.820
of Voldemort's child.

00:04:26.820 --> 00:04:31.470
There was also an interesting tease that Jacob
may not have been completely obliviated at

00:04:31.470 --> 00:04:35.220
the end of the movie after Queenie kissed
him and shielded him with her magic umbrella

00:04:35.220 --> 00:04:36.790
after he stepped out into the rain.

00:04:36.790 --> 00:04:41.290
After all, he seemed to recognise her when
he saw her in his bakery where he'd made lots

00:04:41.290 --> 00:04:43.660
of cakes in the shape of the fantastic beasts.

00:04:43.660 --> 00:04:47.930
Dan Fogler, the actor who plays Jacob, has
hinted that his character has likely been

00:04:47.930 --> 00:04:52.960
affected by all the magic he's been in contact
with such as being bitten by a murtlap, eating

00:04:52.960 --> 00:04:56.650
magical strudel, and being treated with Newt's
potions.

00:04:56.650 --> 00:05:01.340
And although Newt, Tina, Queenie and Jacob
are all confirmed to appear in the next movie,

00:05:01.340 --> 00:05:04.940
producer David Heyman believes that they may
not be at "the heart of all" the movies.

00:05:04.940 --> 00:05:08.850
In fact, it seems that in the next film it
will actually be Credence and Grindelwald

00:05:08.850 --> 00:05:10.660
who "will be the main players".

00:05:10.660 --> 00:05:14.470
All of this means it looks like in the sequel
we're going to be getting more emphasis on

00:05:14.470 --> 00:05:17.230
building the struggle between Dumbledore and
Grindelwald.

00:05:17.230 --> 00:05:21.710
It's more like the Harry vs Voldemort conflict
from the Harry Potter franchise.

00:05:21.710 --> 00:05:26.690
So, although the beasts will be taking something
of a back seat in the sequel, director David

00:05:26.690 --> 00:05:31.850
Yates has confirmed they are planning on introducing
some new beasts, including a particularly

00:05:31.850 --> 00:05:34.000
special Chinese fantastic beast.

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:38.220
So, guys, what do you think about the deleted
scenes and do you think any of them should

00:05:38.220 --> 00:05:39.220
have stayed in the movie?

00:05:39.220 --> 00:05:41.740
And what would you like to see happen in the
sequel?

00:05:41.740 --> 00:05:43.420
Do let me know in the comments below.

